WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:01.968
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:02.969
"The Tonight Show,"

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.103
coming to you live here.

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:06.239
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.207
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:11.177
Well, guys, in public,
President Trump hasn't given up

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.279
on the election,
but the big story is,

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.980
in private,
he's been telling people

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:16.416
he wants to start his own

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:19.919
right-wing conservative media
network to take on Fox News.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.521
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.823
Finally, a chance to hear
what Trump has to say.

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:26.359
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.695
Yeah, Trump wants
to take on Fox News.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.697
Let me just say,
good luck trying to replicate

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:32.899
the electricity
that is Neil Cavuto.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.669 line:0%
Seriously, you're going to try
to beat this Lou Dobbs bit?

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:40.139 line:0%
-The caravan, of mostly
Central American immigrants,

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:42.074 line:0%
is now in the Mexican city

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:43.876 line:0%
of "Hualjeda" tonight.
[ Huixtla ]

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:45.745
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.546
-Good luck.
Good luck.

00:00:47.546 --> 00:00:50.550
This is fun -- the Trump network
already has the catchy slogan...

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.186 line:0%
[ As Trump ]

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.954 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:57.023
That's right, Trump
will base his new network

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:59.125
in the media capital
of the world --

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:02.628
the Four Seasons Total
Landscaping in Philadelphia.

00:01:02.628 --> 00:01:05.765
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.267
Listen to this --
I heard that Joe Biden

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:10.136
is going to stop building
Trump's border wall.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.238
Yep, and that, after four years,

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.841
Trump only got 12 miles
of new wall built.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:16.809
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:18.377
Mexico is like, "12 miles?

00:01:18.377 --> 00:01:19.612
We'll pay for that."

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.447
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:22.615
What's your Venmo?

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.116
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.116 --> 00:01:26.285
When history looks back
at presidential accomplishments,

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:29.389
everyone will remember
the New Deal, Social Security,

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:31.224
and Trump's 12 miles
of border wall.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:32.458
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:33.760
12 miles? I've shopped

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.194
at Costcos bigger than that.

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:39.365
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.701
Trump's like a dad who promises
to build the tree house

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.502
and, now, there's just a pile
of wood in the backyard

00:01:43.502 --> 00:01:45.771
and three rungs of a ladder
going up the tree.

00:01:45.771 --> 00:01:48.641
It's like, "You're too old
for a tree, anyway."

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.176
I wasn't when you started.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.577
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:54.080
Yep, president-elect Biden
is already getting to work.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.582
He's starting to select members
for his cabinet

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:57.816
and, last night, he filled

00:01:57.816 --> 00:01:59.485
an important role.
Watch this.

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:02.254 line:0%
-Overnight, Joe Biden making
his first major decision

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:05.257 line:0%
as president-elect,
naming his right-hand man,

00:02:05.257 --> 00:02:07.392 line:0%
tapping long-time adviser
Ron Klain

00:02:07.392 --> 00:02:09.128 line:0%
to be his chief of staff.

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:10.463
-And, if everything goes well,

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:12.599
you'll never hear
that guy's name again.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:16.402
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.371
When Klain moves
into his office,

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.340
he'll find a desk, two chairs,

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.275
and 50 empty bottles of whiskey.

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:23.275
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.275 --> 00:02:24.377
When Trump heard Biden

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:26.112
hired a chief of staff,
he was like --

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:28.848
[ As Trump ]
Ah, yes, you always
remember your first.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:30.950
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:33.886
Actually, I don't.
What was -- Who was my first?

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:35.554
Was it Reince Prius?

00:02:35.554 --> 00:02:37.257
[ Laughter ]
Reese's Pieces?

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:39.025
[ Laughter ]
Reince?

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:40.926
Trump was like --
[ As Trump ] Don't worry.
If it's not a great fit,

00:02:40.926 --> 00:02:42.662
you can always hire three more.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.896
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:46.132
Trump's had four chiefs
of staff.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:47.533
One quit, one was fired,

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:49.902
one has COVID,
and the fourth went out

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:51.470
to get a pack of cigarettes
and never came back.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:55.608
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.543
Of course, people are still
talking about the election.

00:02:57.543 --> 00:02:59.245
Trump still refuses to concede,

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:01.580
even though there's been
no proof of voter fraud.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:02.848
Meanwhile, Trump's supporters

00:03:02.848 --> 00:03:04.250
are planning
to flood Washington, D.C.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.552
to protest Biden's election.

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:08.688
Also, there's --
-Man, I'm tired of the news.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:12.891
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.891 --> 00:03:15.161
-What was that, Tariq?

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:16.929
-I said I'm tired
of the news, man.

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:18.998
It's always so upsetting.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.600
Can we talk about something
not in the news?

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.669
-Fine with me.
What do you want to talk about?

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:25.338
-I don't know.

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:29.608
What's like the most random,
harmless thing?

00:03:29.608 --> 00:03:31.510
How about doorbells?

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.379
-Sure, love doorbells.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.513
They're on doors.

00:03:34.513 --> 00:03:36.182
You push them and --

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.383
♪♪

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.351
I'm sorry, Tariq.
We just got breaking news.

00:03:39.351 --> 00:03:41.654
[ Laughter ]
-What is it?

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:47.126 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
-What?!

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:50.029
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.064
Okay, fine.
Let's talk about something else.

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:53.766
How about lettuce?

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.501
-Sure, sure.
I love lettuce.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.637
Iceberg, chopped, Romaine --

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:58.938
♪♪

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:01.273
Sorry, Tariq,
We have more breaking news.

00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:02.842
-Please don't read it.
-I have to.

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:07.380
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.714
I have to.
It's my job.

00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:10.083
I'm a comedy news person.

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:12.385
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.388 --> 00:04:17.623
-Oh, come on!

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:19.625
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:20.960
How about dogs?

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.496
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.034 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.034 --> 00:04:30.036 line:0%
-Coffee mugs?

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:32.105 line:0%
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:37.677 line:0%
-Ahh!

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:39.478
All the news is so bad,

00:04:39.478 --> 00:04:41.880
you might as well just go back
to talking about voter fraud.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.148
-No, no.
Come on.

00:04:43.148 --> 00:04:44.250
What do you want to talk about?

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.551
-I don't know.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:47.987
What's the most
random thing ever?

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:51.757
Um, how about that rare bird
from New Zealand,

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:53.726
the kiwi pukupuku?

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:55.561
[ Laughter ]
-I would love to talk

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:58.231
about the kiwi pukupuku,
instead of voter fraud.

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:00.133
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:08.975 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.076
-I give up, man.

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:11.444
I'll just go back
to not listening

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:13.045
to your monologue, as usual.

00:05:13.045 --> 00:05:14.280
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.282
-What?

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:17.583
-Hmm?

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.117
-Tariq Trotter, everyone.
Tariq --

00:05:19.117 --> 00:05:20.419
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:22.854
Tariq Trotter!
Tariq Trotter, everyone!

00:05:22.854 --> 00:05:28.527
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:28.527 --> 00:05:31.597
Uh, hey listen to this.

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:33.532
Ticketmaster is working
on new plans

00:05:33.532 --> 00:05:34.834
to make concerts safe

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.869
during the COVID era.
Check it out.

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:39.005 line:0%
-According to Billboard,
fans who need to prove

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:41.340 line:0%
they've been vaccinated
or tested negative

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.242 line:0%
24 hours before an event.

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:46.278 line:0%
Their status would appear
on the Ticketmaster app.

00:05:46.278 --> 00:05:48.247
-Come on. Half the fun
of going to a concert

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.749
is not knowing what
you're going to catch.

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:51.417
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:52.951
It backfires when you see
sketchy guys

00:05:52.951 --> 00:05:55.221
selling negative COVID tests
outside the arena.

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:58.357
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.357 --> 00:06:00.059
Yep, so, now, when you're
passing around a joint

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.593
with strangers
at a music festival,

00:06:01.593 --> 00:06:02.594
you can finally think,

00:06:02.594 --> 00:06:03.830
"This is safe."

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:07.433
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:08.801
Yeah, I heard that,
after the election,

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:11.370
one industry got a big boost.
Take a look at this.

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.140 line:0%
-Liquor store owners
in Washington, D.C. say

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:18.010 line:0%
they saw more champagne sold
on Saturday, November 7th,

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.345 line:0%
than on the past two

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:22.047 line:0%
New Year's Eve
celebrations combined.

00:06:22.047 --> 00:06:23.782
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:23.782 --> 00:06:25.084
-You can tell things
are going well

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:26.818
because, when they heard,
the champagne industry

00:06:26.818 --> 00:06:28.354
had nothing
to celebrate with.

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:31.991
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:33.359
I'll let you get there.

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:35.161
I'll let you get there, yeah.

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:37.363
Yep, the champagne industry
has been struggling

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:39.031
during the pandemic,
which makes sense,

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:41.233
because no one's ever been like,
"I took a shower

00:06:41.233 --> 00:06:42.635
and put on pants."

00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:46.138
[ Pop ]
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:48.373
[ Laughter intensifies ]

00:06:48.373 --> 00:06:50.476
That's the sound effect
we got for the champagne?

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:52.912
[ Laughter ]
[ Pop ]

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:56.649
Man.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:58.851
It's usually more like a --
"Whsss!" you know, like that.

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:00.586
It's like --
[ Pop ]

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:01.654
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:04.690
-Sssss! Sssss!
-Congratulations.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:05.891
It's like the most
boring champagne.

00:07:05.891 --> 00:07:09.428
Probably like, "Dude,
we just won $80 million!"

00:07:09.428 --> 00:07:13.065
[ Pop ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:15.901
-This bottle
of champagne is flat!

00:07:15.901 --> 00:07:18.871
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:20.205
-Wow.

00:07:20.205 --> 00:07:21.741
Clean, clean pop!

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:23.508
[ Laughter ]

00:07:23.508 --> 00:07:24.576
Well, this made me laugh.

00:07:24.576 --> 00:07:26.678
A statue in Spain --
Did you see this?

00:07:26.678 --> 00:07:28.580
-Yes. Yes.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:30.449
-Classic.
-This is unbelievable.

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:32.518
A statue in Spain is getting
a lot of attention

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:35.187
after a botched restoration.

00:07:35.187 --> 00:07:36.822
Take a look
at the statue before.

00:07:36.822 --> 00:07:38.524
This is real.

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:40.459
Then it got restored.
Here it is after.

00:07:40.459 --> 00:07:43.929
[ Laughter ]
-Yes! Yes!

00:07:43.929 --> 00:07:45.431
-Oh!

00:07:45.431 --> 00:07:46.932
-I love to see it.

00:07:46.932 --> 00:07:48.000
[ Pop ]

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.202
[ Laughter ]
Oh, yeah.

00:07:50.202 --> 00:07:52.471
Meanwhile, the gargoyle
around the corner was like --

00:07:52.471 --> 00:07:53.606
[ Smoker's voice ]
I'd still hit that.

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:56.542
[ Laughter ]
Hey, wait, come on.

00:07:56.542 --> 00:07:59.445
No.

00:07:59.445 --> 00:08:00.913
It's like the difference
between working

00:08:00.913 --> 00:08:02.080
for "Restorations"

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.116
and "Restorations
Total Landscaping."

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:05.484
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.484 --> 00:08:06.719
Can we take another look
at the statue

00:08:06.719 --> 00:08:08.587
before it was restored?

00:08:08.587 --> 00:08:10.022
And now the new one again?

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:11.557
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.557 --> 00:08:12.958
Jeez.

00:08:12.958 --> 00:08:14.993
Well, a lot of people are
speaking out about the update,

00:08:14.993 --> 00:08:17.563
including the statues
themselves.

00:08:17.563 --> 00:08:20.766
[ Laughter ]

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:22.468
First, the original
statue said...

00:08:26.705 --> 00:08:27.940
The new statue said...

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:32.211
[ Hello! That hurts my feelings.
I'm beautiful! ]

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:35.515
[ Laughter ]
Then, the original statue
was like...

00:08:39.252 --> 00:08:40.552
Then, the new statue was like...

00:08:40.552 --> 00:08:44.156
[ No! I like my face!
You're just jealous! ]

00:08:44.156 --> 00:08:45.958
[ Laughter ]

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:48.260
Then, the Jesus painting
from Borja, Spain,

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:49.595
spoke up and said...

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:53.165
[ Yeah! Leave her alone!
She's perfect! ]

00:08:53.165 --> 00:08:56.969
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:56.969 --> 00:08:59.905
Then, this old statue of the
Fonz showed up and was like,

00:08:59.905 --> 00:09:02.208
"Errrrr!"
[ Laughter ]

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:06.412
[ I agree!
Don't change for anyone! ]

00:09:06.412 --> 00:09:08.814
And, finally, this plaque
of Elvis Presley said...

00:09:08.814 --> 00:09:12.317
[ Keep your head up!
You're a hunka hunka
burning love! ]

00:09:12.317 --> 00:09:14.086
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:09:14.086 --> 00:09:15.554
They're all very supportive.

00:09:15.554 --> 00:09:17.757
And, finally, the holiday
season is almost here.

00:09:17.757 --> 00:09:19.191
You guys psyched
for the holidays?

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:21.827
[ Cheering and applause ]
We're going to make it good.

00:09:21.827 --> 00:09:24.463
Well, a Christmas tree
in Cincinnati's Fountain Square

00:09:24.463 --> 00:09:25.631
has been getting a lot
of attention

00:09:25.631 --> 00:09:28.734
for its unique look.
Here it is.

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:31.237
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:32.638
-Yeah.
When asked about the tree,

00:09:32.638 --> 00:09:34.473
the statue from Spain said,

00:09:34.473 --> 00:09:37.243
"Ermahgerd!
That tree looks perferct!"

00:09:37.243 --> 00:09:39.111
♪ Er, Christmas tree ♪

00:09:39.111 --> 00:09:41.113
♪ Er, Christmas tree ♪

00:09:41.113 --> 00:09:42.581
♪ Er there's yer birds ♪

00:09:42.581 --> 00:09:44.550
♪ Er branches ♪

